entityDescription:
According to the document Statut:

The Academy of Silesia, hereinafter referred to as the "University" or "AS", is a non-public University established on the basis of a permit granted by the decision of the Minister of National Education and Sport of December 15, 2003, No. DSW-3-4011-352/TT/03.
2. The founder of the University is Mr. Arkadiusz Hotda.
3. The University operates on the basis of the Act of July 20, 2018 - the Law on Higher Education and Science (Journal of Laws 2018, item 1668, as amended), hereinafter referred to as the Act, regulations issued on its basis and this statute.
4. The seat of the University is the city of Katowice.
5. The University has legal personality!!,
1) conducting education at university;
2) conducting education at postgraduate studies or other forms of education;
3) conducting scientific activities, providing research services and transferring knowledge and technology to the economy;
4) conducting education of doctoral students;
5) educating and promoting university staff;
6) creating conditions for disabled persons to participate in:- the process of admission to the university for the purpose of education,- education,- conducting scientific activities;
7) educating students in a sense of responsibility for the Polish state, the traditions of nations<1-, strengthening the principles of democracy and respect for human rights;
8) creating conditions for the development of physical culture of students; 9) popularizing and increasing the achievements of science and culture, including through collecting and making library, information and archive collections available;
10) acting for the benefit of local and regional communities;
I I) conducting scientific research and development work, artistic creation and providing research, advisory and expert services;
1. The University is an academic University.
2. The University conducts first, second and third cycle studies, uniform master's studies, postgraduate studies and training courses or other forms of education.
3. The University conducts doctoral education.
4. The University is authorized to conduct proceedings and award the degree of doctor in scientific disciplines in which it has obtained the appropriate competences under separate regulations.5. The University is authorized to conduct proceedings and award the degree of habilitated doctor in scientific disciplines in which it has obtained the appropriate competences under separate regulations. 6. The University may organize seminars, conferences, congresses and exhibitions.

